--------------------- CableDyn Input File ------------------------------------
CableDyn driver deck -- Rigid6 spar with a fixed hull rod and two pinned outrigger rods, waves, dynamic
-- A 6 m diameter spar floats in 150 m of water. Body 1 is a free Rigid6 body that carries the
-- ballast (mass, centre of gravity, and inertia; Volume = 0). The hull is rod 1, a Body1 rod fixed
-- in the body frame from 60 m draft to 10 m freeboard: its submerged length gives the buoyancy
-- and the waterplane restoring, and its mass and Morison loads are lumped into the body. Rods 2
-- and 3 are Body1Pinned outriggers: End A is pinned to the keel, each rod has its own three
-- rotations, and it loads the spar only through the pin force. Each outrigger tip (R2B, R3B)
-- carries a polyester tether to an anchor; three studless chain catenaries run from fairleads at
-- 20 m draft. The static solve (bodyIC static) balances the spar, the outriggers, and all lines
-- in the 0.4 m/s current; the regular 4 m, 8 s Airy wave is then ramped in over 20 s.
